{
  "description": "The pack a download requests and where it turns on each answer. The envelope's deltas are the deltas that exist. A device with a base, the bundle it runs, takes the delta the envelope lists for that base whenever a file is missing, one included. A device without a base takes the full pack. The delta route is a GET on the updates host, {updatesBaseUrl}/v1/apps/{appId}/bundles/{bundleId}/deltas/{baseBundleId}. A device with a base the envelope lists no delta for sends it once and never retries it, then takes the full pack. It requests the full pack without waiting for the route's answer and reads nothing of that answer, so no answer and no failure of the route changes the download. The device tries the packs in order. A pack serves the download when it answers 200 or 206, its read ends without a refusal or a failure of the device, and no file is missing after it. No redirect is followed. Any problem with a delta leads to the full pack: an answer other than 200 or 206, no answer from the network, a pack that arrives and is refused for a broken archive, a length that is off or an entry that does not verify, a patch entry that does not apply, or a file still missing after it. A failure of the device itself, a write that fails on its storage or memory that runs out while a file inflates, starts no fallback and fails the download with download_failed. Apart from it, only a failed full pack fails the download, and with the full pack's own reason: download_failed for an error answer or no answer, content_mismatched for a full pack that arrives and is refused or leaves a listed file missing. answers are the answers to the pack requests in order, each { missingFileCount, readOutcome, status }. status is the HTTP status of the last answer after the retries, null when the network gave no answer. readOutcome says how the read of the pack ended: pack_read, pack_refused for a pack that arrived and was refused, or device_failed when the device itself failed, null when the answer was not 200 or 206. missingFileCount counts the files still missing after a pack_read, null otherwise. deltaRouteAnswer is { status }, what the delta route answered, its status null for no answer, and null when the device does not ask the route. deltaRouteUrl is the URL of the delta route the device asks, null when it asks none. requests are the packs requested, in order. downloadedEvent is what the downloaded event carries, the kind and length of the pack that served the download, so after a delta that failed it names the full pack and counts its bytes alone. It is null when the device sends none: no file was missing, or the download failed. failedReason is the reason the download failed with, null when it did not fail.",
